{
  "version": 2,
  "_doc": "Service catalogue for urban programmes. One entry = one building role. count = 0 below minPop, else 1 when per = 0, else clamp(floor(pop / per), 1, max). area = useful m2 per site, interpolated between area[0] and area[1] by log10(pop / minPop) / 2 (perCapita overrides it, clamped to area). site: nucleus | gate | waterfront | river (mills: river front, else any shore) | quay (port: in a town whose plan has quay streets, only a block a quay serves (roles::site_admissible), and the quays' quarters form the port district; without quays, sea or lake shore first, then river) | downstream (lowest river reach) | hill | edge | spread. maxPop (optional) drops the entry above that population. requires: water = only on a waterfront block. function stays one of the six houses functions (market/common are the open_space demands). district = preferred district role prefix. The nucleus table maps catalogue.json cultures[c].nucleus.kind to the role that becomes the central landmark.",
  "_docStates": "Programme context state. decay = share of built allocations given the suffix (households 0, label suffix); a declining town raises its dwelling demand by 1/(1-decay) so the living population keeps its homes and the surplus stands empty.",
  "states": {
    "thriving": { "decay": 0, "suffix": "", "label": "" },
    "declining": { "decay": 0.2, "suffix": ".abandoned", "label": " à l’abandon" },
    "abandoned": { "decay": 1, "suffix": ".abandoned", "label": " à l’abandon" },
    "ruined": { "decay": 1, "suffix": ".ruin", "label": " en ruine" }
  },
  "_docIsolated": "Programme context roles for a single structure (no town): one intent on one unsubdivided domain.",
